Yes, although as it dried it'd actually get pretty sticky. 

One reason not to have it would be the difficulty in applying it 
reasonably: if I belt a grid bug with a quarterstaff, how much gore 
covers me? What about the difference between a dagger and a 
two-handed sword against a giant? Are vampires full of blood, or 
essentially bloodless?

another: towels aren't /that/ common, so if gore accumlated 
'realistically', then many characters would be weaponless for much 
of the early game - unless, perhaps, additional functionality were 
added to sinks/fountains/pools "You feel much refreshed".

It might be an interesting addition to the mechanics of the game if 
well done, otherwise it'd just be a royal pain in the arse [not 
enough, by itself, to exclude it from consideration, mind you].

